for λ1 (M ) and an eigenvector for λ2 (M ).
Proof. Let v1 , . . . , vn be an orthonormal eigenbasis of M , with corresponding eigenvalues λ1 ≥
· · · ≥ λn , and let P = xxT + yyT . Then P is the orthogonal projector onto span{x, y}. Put
ci = ∥P vi ∥2 . Since 0 ≤ ci ≤ 1 and i ci = tr P = 2,
