Taking x = v1 and y = v2 proves the variational formula. Suppose that λ1 is simple. Then
λ1 > λ2 , so equality in the last inequality forces c1 = 1, equivalently v1 ∈ span{x, y}. Equality in
the preceding inequality forces the remaining line of this span to lie in the eigenspace of λ2 . The
converse is immediate.

