Lemma 2.2. Let p, q, c be positive integers with p + q + c = n. Then B(K(n, p, q)) has rank three,
and its nonzero eigenvalues are the roots of t3 − nt2 + pqt + cpq = 0. Two are positive and the third
is −τ for some τ > 0. Moreover,

                        S2 (K(n, p, q)) = n − 2 + τ,      τ 3 + nτ 2 + pqτ = cpq.

