A calculation gives det(tI3 − Q) = t3 − nt2 + pqt + cpq and det Q = −pqc ̸= 0. Since B(K(n, p, q))
has three row types, its rank is at most 3. Because det Q ̸= 0, its rank is exactly 3, and its nonzero
eigenvalues are precisely those of Q.
    These eigenvalues are real, have product det Q = −pqc < 0, and sum tr Q = n > 0. Hence two
are positive and one is negative; write the latter as −τ (τ > 0). The two positive eigenvalues are
the two largest eigenvalues of B(K(n, p, q)), so

                        S2 (K(n, p, q)) = S2 (B(K(n, p, q))) − 2 = n − 2 + τ.

Substitution of t = −τ into t3 − nt2 + pqt + cpq = 0 yields τ 3 + nτ 2 + pqτ = cpq.

