     The same lemma shows that B    b has two positive eigenvalues and one negative eigenvalue −τn .
Since U is a maximizing two-dimensional subspace for B,    b it is the positive spectral subspace. Let
w be a unit eigenvector for −τn . Since w = −τn−1 Bw,
                                                    b    it belongs to the image of B b and is therefore
constant on each part. Denote its values on the p-, q-, and c-parts by wp , wq , wc , respectively. The
first two coordinates of Bwb = −τn w give

                          (p + τn )wp + cwc = 0,           (q + τn )wq + cwc = 0.
Since p, q, c, τn > 0, these equations show that wp , wq , wc are all nonzero.
   The vectors x, y, w form an orthonormal basis of the space of vectors that are constant on the
three parts. The normalized characteristic vectors of the three parts form another orthonormal
basis of the same space. Since the sum of the outer products of an orthonormal basis depends only
on the subspace, for distinct vertices within the p-, q-, and c-parts, respectively,
                                1                     1                      1
                        κuv =     − wp2 ,     κuv =     − wq2 ,      κuv =     − wc2 .
                                p                     q                      c
Moreover, pwp2 + qwq2 + cwc2 = 1. Since all three terms are positive, each of the preceding three
quantities is positive.
